  "formula": {
    "tex": "\\begin{aligned}\\term{compactness}{C}&=\\dfrac{4\\pi\\term{area}{A}}{\\term{perimeter}{P}^2},\\quad\\term{schwartzberg}{S}=\\sqrt{\\term{compactness}{C}},\\quad\\term{convexity}{V}=\\min\\left(\\dfrac{\\term{area}{A}}{\\term{hull-area}{H}},1\\right)\\\\\\term{elongation}{E}&=1-\\sqrt{\\dfrac{\\term{minor}{\\lambda_2}}{\\term{major}{\\lambda_1}}},\\quad\\term{sliver}{F}=\\mathbb{1}\\left[\\term{perimeter}{P}>0\\land(\\term{area}{A}\\le0\\lor\\term{compactness}{C}<\\term{threshold}{\\tau})\\right]\\end{aligned}",
    "ascii": "Polsby-Popper C=4*pi*A/P^2; Schwartzberg S=sqrt(C); convexity V=min(A/H,1) for hull area H; elongation E=1-sqrt(lambda2/lambda1) with lambda2=max(mean-radius,0), lambda1=mean+radius from central moments. Sliver is P>0 and (A<=0 or C<threshold). C and S are NaN unless A>0 and P>0, V is NaN without positive hull area, E is NaN without a positive major eigenvalue. Shells contribute positive area and holes negative, regardless of winding.",
